Engine: editor debugging on non-Windows platforms through files

The engine only created an editor debugger on Windows (named pipes); elsewhere
--enabledebugger quit with "editor_debugger is NULL", and breaking into the
debugger and reporting script errors were compiled out. FileBasedAGSDebugger
already existed but was unused.

The command line option "--debugger-comm <pipe|file>" selects how the engine
talks to the editor: named pipes (Windows only, as before) or
FileBasedAGSDebugger on every platform, which exchanges its files
(dbgsend.tmp / dbgrecv.tmp) in the folder given as the instance token and
writes messages atomically (temporary file + rename). Without the option the
platform default is used: pipes on Windows, files elsewhere.
break_into_debugger() and send_exception_to_debugger() work on all platforms;
only SetForegroundWindow stays Windows-specific.

Used by ags4mac (macOS editor port) for breakpoints and stepping.
Branch engine-file-debugger-non-windows (two commits), adventuregamestudio/ags#3159.

